    "disclaimer-type": "text",
    "disclaimer": "<p>References</p>\r\n<p>1. The American Cancer Society. ‘Key Statistics for Breast Cancer.’ Last Revised: September 14, 2023. Accesssed October 2, 2023 via https://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/breast-cancer/about/how-common-is-breast-cancer.html</p>\r\n<p>2. &nbsp;‘Highlights of prescribing information, SPY AGENT GREEN.’ Accessed 1 October 2023.&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/211580s006lbl.pdf\">https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/211580s006lbl.pdf</a></p>\r\n<p>3. Weintritt, D. “A Study Assessing the Safety and Effectiveness of IC2000 and SPY Fluorescence Imaging Systems (SPY-PHI) in the Visualization of Lymphatic Vessels and Identification of Lymph Nodes During Sentinel Lymph Node Biopsy in Subjects With Breast Cancer (FILM-B).”&nbsp;<i>CTG Labs - NCBI</i>, clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT03200704. Accessed 12 Oct. 2023.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>4. Breastcancer.org. ‘Benefits and drawbacks of sentinel lymph node dissection.’ Accessed 1 October 2023.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.breastcancer.org/treatment/surgery/lymph-node-removal/sentinel-node-dissection/benefits-drawbacks\">https://www.breastcancer.org/treatment/surgery/lymph-node-removal/sentinel-node-dissection/benefits-drawbacks</a></p>\r\n<p>*SPY-PHI technology includes the SPY-PHI Imaging Systems and SPY AGENT® GREEN (indocyanine green for injection).</p>\r\n",
    "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Oct 25 2023 14:51:28 GMT+0000",
